WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.500
The dashboard starts with a KPI row — everything that needs you today: open tickets, SLA at risk, overdue, unassigned, approvals and work due.

2
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.500
Ten sections in one sidebar: Dashboard, My Work, Service Desk, Clients, Assets & Network, Business, Knowledge & Vault, Security & Monitoring and Reports. Administration is pinned at the foot.

3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.500
Short on width? Collapse it to an icon rail and each section opens as a flyout — by mouse or keyboard.

4
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:31.000
Ctrl+K opens Go to: pages, settings, commands, clients, tickets, devices and documents, each searched with its own permission rules. Passwords are never searched.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Open a client and it becomes a workspace: a KPI row, renewals, open invoices and quick actions, with tickets, assets, contracts and more on tabs.

6
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The client's tickets, without leaving the client.

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.500
A service desk you own, not one you rent. Every client in one queue.

8
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:55.800
A ticket that already knows the customer — active contract, hours used, and the SLA countdown.

9
00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.600
Internal notes stay internal. Client-visible replies are kept visibly separate.

10
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.600
The credentials this job needs, by title and username only. Secrets are never rendered here.

11
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.100
The physical network, drawn. A switch rendered from its manufacturer layout, every port coloured by VLAN.

12
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:18.600
Document a port in place. Click it on the artwork: mode, VLANs, PoE and the cable to the patch panel.

13
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.600
Trace the cable from switch port to desk, through the patch panel and the wall jack.

14
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.600
The runbook lives beside the work, linked from the ticket that needed it.

15
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.600
Light or dark, per person. Professional Dark is the default; every screen honours the theme you pick. Per-client documentation and a shared knowledge base, searchable.

16
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:40.600
The asset inventory per client: identity, network, OS, warranty and lifecycle in one list.

17
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:48.400
The asset record: identity, network, OS, hardware, rack position, warranty and lifecycle.

18
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.400
Lifecycle and warranty dates mean the refresh conversation happens before the hardware fails.

19
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:58.900
What is physically in the comms room — every device at its U position, linked to its asset record.

20
00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:04.400
Front-to-rear port mapping. Each panel port: what it is patched from, the permanent link behind it, and where it ends.

21
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.400
Diagrams drawn from the records — connectivity and VLANs, never hand-drawn and never stale.

22
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:14.900
Address space per client: subnets with VLAN, gateway and DNS, and which addresses are free.

23
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.900
The vault: AES-GCM encrypted at rest, per-entry access rules, audited reveals.

24
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:27.400
Dispatch the week. Drag a ticket onto a technician's row; SLA risk surfaces at the top.

25
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:32.900
Recurring maintenance runs on its own schedule, with per-task sign-off.

26
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:41.200
Projects with real dependencies. Drag a bar to reschedule; blocked work says so, and by what.

27
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.200
The dependency table underneath is where the blocking relationships are edited.

28
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.200
The commercial side. Draft, sent and accepted quotes across every client.

29
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:56.700
Quote to signature: a PDF, an email, and a signing link the customer uses without an account.

30
00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:03.200
Every invoice line carries its origin, so a billing query is answerable without reconstructing it.

31
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.700
Agreements track themselves: block hours with rollover, auto-renewal, and a profitability snapshot.

32
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:15.200
Revenue against cost of delivery, per client, drawn from logged time and issued invoices.

33
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:21.200
Client health combines SLA performance, ticket velocity, billing aging and engagement.

34
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:27.200
And the whole book of business: every tenant, every site, on one page.

35
00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.700
Administration opens the settings center: ten categories, searchable, each listing only the pages you may open.

36
00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:38.200
Modules are opt-in. The service desk, AI assistance and the rest stay off until you turn them on.
